# P-locks on the Tonic (wip195): on a voice page (ENV, LFO, EDIT x2, SEL pitch mod, FX mix) hold a step and turn
# a knob: that step gets its own value (one step of the knob's lane); a tap still toggles. SAVE + the knob,
# holding the step, clears it. The SEQ page locks nothing. (Before 195 no page took a lock: V_PART is not
# reached on the Tonic.)
wait 300
expect view 7
expect part 0
expect sound0.0.0 0
expect sound0.0.11 0
expect sound0.1.18 0
# taps on empty steps: on at once (track 1 = the kick, steps 1 and 5)
tapkey w0
tapkey w4
expect hit0.0.0 1
expect hit0.0.4 1
# ENV page (wave K1): hold step 5, turn K1: its own wave; the knob's stays; a lane is born
tap ENV
expect view 12
key w4 down
spin K1 1
key w4 up
expect hit0.0.4 1
expect sound0.0.0 0
expect lanes 1
expect laneval0.0.0.4 1
expect laneval0.0.0.0 255
# a second knob of the same page: Pitch (K2): its own lane
key w4 down
spin K2 10
key w4 up
expect lanes 2
expect sound0.0.1 60
expect laneval0.0.1.0 255
# LFO page: noise filter mode K1
tap LFO
expect view 13
key w4 down
spin K1 1
key w4 up
expect lanes 3
expect laneval0.0.7.4 1
# EDIT page: noise envelope mode K1; EDIT again: VEL page, K1 = osc velocity
# (wip238: a track keeps at most 3 lanes: EDIT, VEL, SEL go on track 2, FX on track 3)
tapkey b1
tap EDIT
expect view 14
key w4 down
spin K1 1
key w4 up
expect lanes 4
expect laneval0.1.10.4 1
tap GLO   # wip290: VEL is GLO 1st press
expect view 15
key w4 down
spin K1 5
key w4 up
expect lanes 5
expect sound0.0.18 0
# SEL: pitch mod shape K1
tap SEL
expect view 11
key w4 down
spin K1 1
key w4 up
expect lanes 6
expect laneval0.1.4.4 1
# FX (1st press): mix 1, K1 = Mix
tapkey b2
tap FX
expect view 9
key w4 down
spin K1 5
key w4 up
expect lanes 7
expect sound0.2.13 0
tapkey b0
# held without a knob: the step stays; a tap takes it off, and back on
tap ENV
key w0 down
wait 600
key w0 up
expect hit0.0.0 1
tapkey w0
expect hit0.0.0 0
tapkey w0
expect hit0.0.0 1
# playing: the lock is stored at once and heard on the next pass: step 5 plays wave 1, step 1 the knob's 0
tap PLAY
wait 450
expect playhead0 5
expect motion0.0.0 1
wait 160
expect playhead0 6
expect motion0.0.0 0
# a lock turned while playing: stored at once (step 1, wave K1), heard on the next pass
key w0 down
spin K1 1
key w0 up
expect laneval0.0.0.0 1
tap PLAY
# SAVE + the knob, holding the step: the lock goes (and its lane, when it was the only one)
key w4 down
press SAVE
spin K1 1
release SAVE
key w4 up
expect laneval0.0.0.4 255
expect lanes 7
tap LFO
key w4 down
press SAVE
spin K1 1
release SAVE
key w4 up
expect laneval0.0.7.4 -1
expect lanes 6
expect hit0.0.4 1
# SEQ: holding a drum step and turning a knob locks nothing new
tap SEQ
expect view 7
key w4 down
spin K1 5
key w4 up
expect laneval0.0.7.4 -1
expect lanes 6
